+# VCF 9.0 architecture research
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 using live network requests.
+
+- “Minimum number of ESXi hosts required on vSAN clusters for deployment of VCF Management Domain,” Broadcom Knowledge Base, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993/minimum-number-of-esxi-hosts-required-on.html — confirmed four hosts for the single-availability-zone management cluster and vSAN for this protected scenario.
+- “Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with the versions of its constituent products,” Broadcom Knowledge Base, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html — confirmed that 9.0.0.0 is a supported VCF release whose constituent products are managed as a VCF bill of materials.
+- “Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning,” Broadcom Knowledge Base, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html — confirmed the common 9.0 release convention used for VCF BOM components.
+- “Product Interoperability Matrix — Upgrade Path,” Broadcom, https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade — checked the forward maintenance-release edges from the greenfield 9.0.0.0 baseline and treated upgrade prechecks as a lifecycle concern, not a change to the initial installer spec.
+- “Broadcom Compatibility Guide,” Broadcom, https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ — checked that hardware and vSAN ESA compatibility remain deployment prerequisites; the fixture deliberately supplies capacity but does not invent server certification data.
+
+The live sources informed the design, while the bundled dated snapshot is the deterministic authority for the generated artifact.
